---
scope: src/service/observer/kanban
alignment: unreviewed
description: Reads the project's kanban board for the observer from the location its brain config declares, read-only, returning the board by column, one task's full note, or an unavailable result with its reason.
intent: >
  Lets the observer show the project's kanban board beside the pipeline and
  open any task in full. The board lives as one folder per project, one
  subfolder per column and one note per task. Its location comes from the
  kanban field the project's own brain config declares; the kanban tag comes
  from the newest session's report, and a kanban folder the user passes for
  one project overrides the configured one. Tasks the current session names
  are marked. Reading never writes the brain. When the board cannot be found,
  the result says why with a hint, and nothing else fails.
outcomes:
  desired:
    - The board shows the project's columns Backlog, Todo, In Progress, In Review and Done, each task with its title, slug, priority and tags. Tasks the current session record names are marked.
    - Opening a task by slug returns that task's full note for the detail drawer, and only notes on this project's board can be returned.
    - The board is found in the kanban folder declared by the brain config at the root the newest session reported, read the same way the rest of the server reads that config, under the kanban tag that session reported. A kanban folder the user passes for one named project overrides the configured one for that project only.
    - When the board cannot be found, the result says unavailable with the reason and a hint, whether the brain config is missing or unreadable, declares no kanban field (hint to set it up through the brain config command), names a source this observer cannot read, points at a missing folder, has no board folder for the tag, or no tag was reported. Nothing else in the observer fails.
    - A task note that cannot be parsed shows as a task marked unreadable instead of being dropped, and only that task is affected; the rest of the board still shows.
    - Any brain plugin that stores its board as plain folders is read without knowing which plugin it is, and the brain is never written.
  undesired:
    - Locating the board from the launcher, the project's instructions or a brain folder a session reported instead of the location the brain config declares, or choosing how to read the brain by recognizing which backend it is. Reading the brain config differently from the rest of the server, so the two disagree about it.
    - A guessed or fallback folder, a kanban source the observer cannot read treated as a folder, or a tag reported by an older session or another project, showing another project's board or a stale one as this project's current board.
    - A task read that returns a note outside this project's board, such as through a slug that reaches out of the board's folders.
    - One malformed task note blanking or failing the whole board, or silently vanishing from it.
    - Any write to the brain, including creating, moving or editing a task.
    - A missing or unreadable board crashing the observer or breaking anything beyond its own part of the view.
---
